{:edb/db-before-t 1200 :edb/db-after-t 1201 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534513 50 #inst "2026-10-07T19:17:18.640Z" 13194139534513 true] [17592186184277 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292685 13194139534513 true] [17592186184278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292692 13194139534513 true] [17592186184278 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292699 13194139534513 true] [17592186184709 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534513 true] [17592186184709 1100 "Find the solution of $x^{2} - 2x < 8$." 13194139534513 false] [17592186184709 1100 "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}-2x<8.$" 13194139534513 true] [17592186184709 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x & <8 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x-8 & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-2x-8$ lies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/83e87f616c1e9a74065016df2d6a0bbfac5bcdc8ee9326721b13a2bd8a8f16d4.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x-8<0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2<x<4.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-2,4).$" 13194139534513 true] [17592186184711 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534513 true] [17592186184711 1100 "Find the solution of $-6x^{2} > - 3x$." 13194139534513 false] [17592186184711 1100 "Find the solution of $-6{x}^{2}>-3x.$" 13194139534513 true] [17592186184711 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{x}^{2} & >-3x \\\\ -6{x}^{2}+3x & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-6{x}^{2}+3x$ lies above the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{x}^{2}+3x & =0 \\\\ -3x(2x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/3dff64c74abd4981c69686cbbf7d79fdd49c7a7fde3bb266b2b6e11c441bcf20.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-6{x}^{2}+3x>0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0<x<\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292685 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292686 13194139534513 true] [17592186292685 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292688 13194139534513 true] [17592186292685 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292690 13194139534513 true] [17592186292685 1089 "q-276402" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292685 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534513 true] [17592186292685 1100 "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}-8x<0.$\n\n{{field-1}} $<x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292685 1113 #uuid "c0311ef6-fe92-51b8-a43d-3cc837a8ac32" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292685 1145 "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-8x<0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-8x\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x & =0 \\\\ x(x-8) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=0$ and $x=8,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/8c4acb1db29c8479f946d6d047fe79d9a87d7162de1ff0725e59052f93df85ce.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $0<x<8.$" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292686 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292687 13194139534513 true] [17592186292686 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534513 true] [17592186292686 1041 "field-1" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292686 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292687 13194139534513 true] [17592186292686 1110 #uuid "bbd4924d-570a-559d-b2dc-f56e552f2ee0" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292687 1034 "0" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292687 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534513 true] [17592186292687 1111 #uuid "0fcaa68c-20d1-560a-80a4-8d8d524032ad" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292688 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292689 13194139534513 true] [17592186292688 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534513 true] [17592186292688 1041 "field-2" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292688 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292689 13194139534513 true] [17592186292688 1110 #uuid "a01c1233-e863-5907-aa31-4700b542c890" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292689 1034 "<" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292689 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534513 true] [17592186292689 1111 #uuid "d393db0e-75b4-5c46-834f-a74cc084b33a" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292690 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292691 13194139534513 true] [17592186292690 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534513 true] [17592186292690 1041 "field-3" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292690 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292691 13194139534513 true] [17592186292690 1110 #uuid "49191652-8c7a-52ab-9393-0549495c3b5d" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292691 1034 "8" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292691 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534513 true] [17592186292691 1111 #uuid "cc99565c-080c-5c9b-96d1-0d0f950e06bd" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292692 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292693 13194139534513 true] [17592186292692 1089 "q-276407" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292692 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534513 true] [17592186292692 1100 "Find the solution of $x+3\\ge 2{x}^{2}.$" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292692 1113 #uuid "d17d341f-d303-5767-85ec-0a66ef9ec1ad" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292692 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+3 & \\ge 2{x}^{2} \\\\ -2{x}^{2}+x+3 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}+x+3$ lies **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}+x+3 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-x-3 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}-3x)+(2x-3) & =0 \\\\ x(2x-3)+(2x-3) & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(2x-3) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)(x-\\frac{3}{2}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-1$ and $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/86d7fbea75961bdb83c014ca9febb735e6a1745f71e8e094de416998b2072630.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+x+3\\ge 0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-1\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-1,\\frac{3}{2}].$" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292693 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292694 13194139534513 true] [17592186292693 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292695 13194139534513 true] [17592186292693 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292696 13194139534513 true] [17592186292693 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292697 13194139534513 true] [17592186292693 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292698 13194139534513 true] [17592186292693 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534513 true] [17592186292693 1041 "selection" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292693 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292697 13194139534513 true] [17592186292693 1110 #uuid "b6edfb28-dc7c-5965-a229-4e405703ffe3" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292694 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{3}{2}]\\cup [1,\\infty )" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292694 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534513 true] [17592186292694 1111 #uuid "ca4696f2-7f99-5bb5-a2e6-2f896009a3cc" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292695 1034 "x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},1]" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292695 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534513 true] [17592186292695 1111 #uuid "b39057be-c22a-538e-b6d8-b817efa2b994" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292696 1034 "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [\\frac{3}{2},\\infty )" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292696 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534513 true] [17592186292696 1111 #uuid "4fb63f72-c77c-597e-a6e6-7af09edbaf8c" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292697 1034 "x\\in [-1,\\frac{3}{2}]" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292697 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534513 true] [17592186292697 1111 #uuid "3b55f7bb-d26d-55e3-b17f-7c1623a1c745" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292698 1034 "x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{3}{2}]" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292698 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534513 true] [17592186292698 1111 #uuid "9447c28b-d9a2-5fcb-8884-1bc8b89ca063" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292699 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292700 13194139534513 true] [17592186292699 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292702 13194139534513 true] [17592186292699 1089 "q-276408" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292699 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534513 true] [17592186292699 1100 "Solve the inequality $4{x}^{2}\\le 12x$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in [${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]$" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292699 1113 #uuid "d3f622fb-d8a5-5f8e-a1ab-925800ff1e0b" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292699 1145 "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2} & \\le 12x \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-12x & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=4{x}^{2}-12x$ lies **below** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-12x & =0 \\\\ 4x(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/d81805f304bd45ddd595bd251202226d2b1ced494fe7816d0bc9f17ee8f998a0.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-12x\\le 0,\n$$\n\n \n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **below** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0\\le x\\le 3.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [0,3].$" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292700 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292701 13194139534513 true] [17592186292700 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534513 true] [17592186292700 1041 "field-1" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292700 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292701 13194139534513 true] [17592186292700 1110 #uuid "8572a649-145f-5e57-850c-73e70d41aafb" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292701 1034 "0" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292701 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534513 true] [17592186292701 1111 #uuid "894b802a-63f9-5a6a-bcd2-d93dcfbcdff7" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292702 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292703 13194139534513 true] [17592186292702 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534513 true] [17592186292702 1041 "field-2" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292702 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292703 13194139534513 true] [17592186292702 1110 #uuid "ff9e19c9-79f3-5995-9c26-a1b6ff4d3e07" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292703 1034 "3" 13194139534513 true] [17592186292703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534513 true] [17592186292703 1111 #uuid "aea1369d-d4c7-5774-96ed-e33aece856fc" 13194139534513 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-276402" 17592186292685 "q-276402/field-1" 17592186292686 "q-276402/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" 17592186292687 "q-276402/field-2" 17592186292688 "q-276402/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" 17592186292689 "q-276402/field-3" 1759218629269